    <briefdescription>
<para>Iterates through instructions in a set of blocks in reverse order from the first non-terminator. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>For example (assume all blocks have size n): <ref refid="classanonymous__namespace_02_g_v_n_sink_8cpp_03_1_1_lockstep_reverse_iterator" kindref="compound">LockstepReverseIterator</ref> <ref refid="_m_d5_8cpp_1ac0eafdc9ee161b71e7af98af736952fd" kindref="member">I([B1, B2, B3])</ref>; *I<ndash/> = [B1[n], B2[n], B3[n]]; *I<ndash/> = [B1[n-1], B2[n-1], B3[n-1]]; *I<ndash/> = [B1[n-2], B2[n-2], B3[n-2]]; ...</para>
<para>It continues until all blocks have been exhausted. <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_use" kindref="compound">Use</ref> <computeroutput><ref refid="classanonymous__namespace_02_g_v_n_sink_8cpp_03_1_1_lockstep_reverse_iterator_1a1c19d8d16ee457dda6fed85074c4b02a" kindref="member">getActiveBlocks()</ref></computeroutput> to determine which blocks are still going and the order they appear in the list returned by operator*. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
